From a5d54b8d69b134ffe899e74f8265b5073ee3e413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 10:00:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3: epcs.c driver + mode 'P' diagnostic (firmware-only
 verified)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a per-byte EPCS16 driver against the Phase 2 wb_altasmi_parallel
wrapper at 0xF2000000.  Four public functions:

  epcs_read(addr, len, buf)     — sequential read via shift_bytes pulses
  epcs_read_status()            — RDSR via rd_status level
  epcs_erase_sector(addr)       — WREN + SE + WIP poll (64 KB sector)
  epcs_program_page(addr,n,buf) — WREN + PP + shift loop + WIP poll
                                  (caller must keep n ≤ 256 and not
                                  cross a page boundary; the wrapper
                                  flags illegal_write via sticky bit)

All four share the same handshake primitives (wait_not_busy,
wait_data_valid) and the level-bit-asserted + shift_bytes-pulses-per-
byte protocol verified against rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v's register
map (CTRL / ADDR / DATAIN / STATUS / DATAOUT / ESTAT).

Mode 'P' added to stage2 main dispatcher: reads 64 B from EPCS offset
0x000000 + hex-dumps over UART + prints RDSR + "probe DONE" marker.
Probe length 64 B chosen as a defensive bound — earlier work
(reference-rublock-complexity, Phase 4.1) observed the FPGA
autonomously reconfiguring back to EPCS factory ~hundreds of ms after
CONF_DONE, and 64 B at 115200 8N1 finishes in ~90 ms with margin to
spare.  Extend to a full sector once the autonomous-reconfig cause is
identified and fixed.

Stage2 size: 13908 B (Phase 2 baseline) → 14460 B (+552 B).
Cross-tests still green: test_lutcodec_c 127/127, test_edits_bin 5/5.

HW VERIFICATION OUTSTANDING.  Five JTAG-volatile flash attempts in the
session that landed this patch all showed stage2 booting successfully
(banner + CLK + SDRAM PASS + dispatcher prompt over UART) followed by
autonomous FPGA reconfig back to EPCS page 0 within ~500 ms — i.e.
before any UART command could be dispatched to mode 'P'.  Removing the
cycloneive_rublock primitive from the netlist did NOT change this
behaviour, ruling out the rublock watchdog hypothesis from Phase 4.1.
Real root cause unidentified — candidates include the qsf
INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE setting baking WD option bits into
the .pof regardless of primitive instantiation, default
AUTO_RESTART_CONFIGURATION behavior, or openFPGALoader -r TAP-state
quirks.  Marked for a dedicated debug session with a scope on nCONFIG
and openFPGALoader --verbose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
